# RME branch tariff authority & financial pricing (rule 192)

> **SUPERSEDED IN PART by rule 195 (ACTIVATION-RME-INVOICE-CORRECTION-PREPAYMENT-2,
> 2026-10-21).** Owner D1a: the checker's approval APPLIES the correction in the
> same transaction. Owner D1b: Kasir requests, Admin Klinik approves, Front Office
> holds both — granted through `RoleSeeder`; no operational role holds
> `apply_rme_invoice_correction` (recovery path only). Owner D1c: the capability is
> confined to SPN4 by a source-controlled, fail-closed allowlist. Any statement
> below that "no role" holds a correction permission, that D1a is undecided, or that
> an approval leaves the invoice untouched until a separate apply is the historical
> record of its release, not current policy. D21c and D21g remain PENDING.

> **SUPERSEDED IN PART by rule 194 — REVISION-RME-MANUAL-PRICING-AUTHORITY-1
> (owner D21 REVISED 2026-10-20: manual cashier pricing, no mandatory tariff).**
> Withdrawn: §1 item 4 (D21 as tariff authority), §2 item 6 ("`mst_tariffs` is
> the price authority" — it is now OPTIONAL REFERENCE), §3 (the default mode is
> MANUAL; STRICT is LEGACY_SUPERSEDED and the strict list is a source-controlled
> empty array — no `RME_TARIFF_STRICT_BRANCH_CODES` override), §4 items 15–16
> (new lines record MANUAL provenance, never TRANSITIONAL / TARIFF_MATCHED), §5
> (tariff exceptions NOT_APPLICABLE), §7 (correction is tariff-independent; no
> `CORRECTION_TARIFF_*`, no STALE `TARIFF_AUTHORITY_CHANGED`) and §11 item 39.
> **Still in force:** §4 item 14 (server arithmetic), §6 D10, §8 tariff audit,
> §9 readiness (informational), §10 roles, and D1/D7.

Evidence: `docs/sprints/feature-rme-branch-tariff-authority-1.md`.
Decision register: `docs/decisions/rme-billing-correction-owner-decisions.md`.
Extends rules 188–191. Where this rule and those disagree about what EXISTS, this rule is newer.

## 1. Owner decisions — OWNER_APPROVED_POLICY (recorded 2026-10-17, task-supplied evidence)
1. **D1** Kasir submits a correction; Admin Klinik approves within its authorized
   branch; Super Admin approves across branches; nobody approves their own
   request — Super Admin included. Enforced already (service, under the invoice
   lock, per account; branch via `RmeWorkingBranchScope`). **The role GRANTS are
   NOT made** — they are the activation ceremony. Who APPLIES (D1a) is undecided.
2. **D7** v0 original preserved, v1… immutable revisions referencing the original,
   its date and reason, nothing overwritten. Already deployed (rule 190 §3).
3. **D10** An invoice with an active correction (SUBMITTED / APPROVED-not-applied)
   accepts no payment; payment resumes after REJECTED / CANCELLED / STALE /
   APPLIED, revalidated against the current version. IMPLEMENTED_THIS_RELEASE.
4. **D21** Prices come from the branch tariff master; overrides/discounts outside
   policy need specific authorization; a branch without complete tariffs keeps
   legacy billing temporarily under auditable transitional controls; correction is
   never activated for lines whose price the tariff cannot validate.
5. Owner approval ≠ repository record ≠ technical enforcement. Never claim the
   third without deployed, verified evidence. Never self-approve a sub-decision.

## 2. Tariff source of truth — IMPLEMENTED_THIS_RELEASE
6. `mst_tariffs` (branch, treatment, effective_date → price) is the price authority.
   `BranchTariffAuthorityService::resolveMany()` is the ONLY resolver: the tariff
   OF THE BRANCH, active, not soft-deleted, `effective_date <= clinical date`
   (latest wins, then highest id), in integer cents. Two queries per invoice.
7. **No cross-branch fallback, ever** — no "same as TLK1". No tariff is invented,
   copied from another branch, or derived from a historical invoice.
8. **A zero tariff is not authority** (D21g / Rp0 undecided) — it resolves to
   `TARIFF_ZERO_PRICE`. An inactive/deleted treatment resolves to
   `TREATMENT_INACTIVE` (except when re-validating an UNCHANGED kept correction
   line, `requireActiveTreatment: false` — rule 190 §11a).
9. The treatment master is GLOBAL: every active treatment is billable in every
   branch. A branch is `TARIFF_READY` only when ALL active treatments have a
   positive tariff in force; some tariffs ⇒ `TARIFF_INCOMPLETE`, never ready.
   **[Extended by rule 193: coverage is not approval.** TARIFF_READY says every
   active treatment has a positive tariff; it says nothing about whether the owner
   approved those prices. Strict eligibility additionally requires every tariff in
   force to carry approval provenance. Production TLK1's 11 tariffs are seeded
   development defaults (UNVERIFIED).]
10. Clinical date comes from `ClinicalClock` (WITA), never `now()` / UTC. No cache:
    a tariff edit is visible on the next resolution, so a stale cache never
    authorizes a price.

## 3. Branch pricing mode — TRANSITIONAL is ACTIVE_IN_PRODUCTION; STRICT_ENFORCEMENT_PENDING
11. Every branch is **TRANSITIONAL** (`TariffPricingMode::TRANSITIONAL`) unless its
    canonical code is listed — then it is `STRICT_ENFORCED` — in
    `config/rme_tariff_authority.php` `strict_branch_codes`
    (environment key `RME_TARIFF_STRICT_BRANCH_CODES`, parsed at config-build time,
    canonicalised through `BranchCodeAlias`, exact-token). Default: none.
12. **Nothing becomes strict because it has tariffs.** Readiness never changes a mode.
    A strict branch that is not ready is a readiness FAIL (its cashiers are refused).
13. Strict is honoured only for an active, RME-enabled branch; anything else —
    including an unknown id — is TRANSITIONAL (never refuses more than legacy did).

## 4. Server-side invoice pricing — IMPLEMENTED_THIS_RELEASE
14. `RmeInvoicePricingService::price()` prices every line of `RmeInvoiceService::create()`:
    **ALL MODES** — integer cents (no floats), qty ≥ 1, price/discount ≥ 0 (legacy
    messages kept), **discount ≤ line gross** (`INVOICE_LINE_NEGATIVE`), overflow of
    decimal(15,2) refused before multiplying (`INVOICE_TOTAL_OVERFLOW`), totals
    recomputed (a submitted total/branch is never read). Priced BEFORE an invoice
    number is drawn.
15. **TRANSITIONAL** keeps the cashier price and records provenance on the line:
    `pricing_mode`, `price_source` ∈ {`TARIFF_MATCHED`, `TRANSITIONAL_TARIFF_DEVIATION`,
    `TRANSITIONAL_NO_TARIFF`, `TRANSITIONAL_FREE_TEXT`}, `tariff_id`,
    `tariff_unit_price` (the tariff AT BILLING TIME — the evidence; a later tariff
    edit never rewrites it). A transitional price is never shown as master tariff.
16. Legacy lines (before this release) keep `price_source = NULL` = "Belum tercatat
    (sebelum otoritas tarif)". **Never backfill provenance.**
17. **STRICT** refuses, with stable codes, audited `RME_INVOICE_PRICING_REFUSED`
    after the rollback (ids + code only, never a typed price):
    `TARIFF_FREE_TEXT_NOT_PERMITTED`, `TARIFF_TREATMENT_INACTIVE`, `TARIFF_MISSING`,
    `TARIFF_ZERO_PRICE`, `TARIFF_PRICE_MISMATCH`, `TARIFF_DISCOUNT_NOT_AUTHORIZED`,
    `TARIFF_EXCEPTION_REASON_REQUIRED`, `TARIFF_RP0_NOT_PERMITTED` (line or total).

## 5. Price / discount exceptions — IMPLEMENTED_THIS_RELEASE, FUTURE_ACTIVATION
18. A strict deviation (`override_rme_tariff_price`) or discount
    (`authorize_rme_tariff_discount`) is accepted only when the switch
    `rme_tariff_authority.price_exceptions_enabled` is ON **and** the actor holds the
    specific permission **and** gives a 10–500 character reason. Recorded as
    `TARIFF_EXCEPTION_AUTHORIZED` with `price_exception_by` / `price_exception_reason`;
    audited with the reason LENGTH only.
19. The switch is **OFF** and **source-controlled** — a literal `false` in
    `config/rme_tariff_authority.php` with **no environment override** (the
    `global_permitted` precedent), so a widening of what a cashier may charge is
    never one host edit away. Both permissions are granted to **NO role**. As
    built, the account creating the invoice authorizes its own exception (no
    maker/checker), so the switch must **not** be opened before D21b supplies a
    separate approver and that step exists. The switch is a plain config value, so
    Super Admin's wildcard grants the permission but **never** opens exceptions.
    Even an authorized exception can never create an Rp0 line or total.
20. PENDING_SUB_DECISIONS D21a–D21i (duration, exception approver, max discount,
    max deviation, thresholds, max override, intrinsically-free treatments, official
    tariff data, tariff date basis). **Never invent a percentage, a cap or an
    approver.** D21i default: the tariff in force on the **invoice's clinical
    date** selects the price, identically at creation and at correction.

## 6. D10 — pending correction blocks payment — IMPLEMENTED_THIS_RELEASE
21. `RmePaymentService::assertNoActiveCorrection()` runs on the LOCKED invoice row,
    after the version check, on all three paths (`pay`, `allocateControlPayment`,
    `allocateVisitPayment`) for every invoice the batch would settle (the paid /
    control / current invoice always; parents and receivables when reached).
22. A hit raises `RmeInvoicePaymentBlocked` (`[INVOICE_CORRECTION_ACTIVE]`): the WHOLE
    batch rolls back (no partial allocation), audited `RME_PAYMENT_REFUSED_ACTIVE_CORRECTION`
    after the rollback (ids, codes, correction id/status, version — never the
    amount, note or reference), surfaced on field `payment_blocked`.
23. Race safety: a correction becomes active only inside a transaction holding the
    same invoice row lock (submit locks the invoice first). Correction first ⇒ the
    payment waits then is refused; cancellation first ⇒ the payment waits then is
    accepted; payment first ⇒ the submission waits then is refused (not pre-payment).
    Proven on PostgreSQL 16 with a competing child process.
24. The payment FormRequest repeats the check unlocked, BEFORE the amount cap, for the
    paid invoice + carry-over parents / selected receivables (stricter, never the
    authority). The payment page and invoice page explain the block and disable the
    action; with no active correction they render exactly as before.
25. **Not flag-gated.** With the flag OFF no correction can become active, so it
    refuses nothing — but a correction left active by a flag switched off still
    blocks. **Resolve (reject/cancel) every active correction before switching the
    flag OFF.**
26. STALE:PAYMENT_RECORDED stays as defence in depth (a payment written by a path that
    bypassed the guard); in the normal flow D10 makes it unreachable.

## 7. D21(4) — correction only within tariff authority — IMPLEMENTED_THIS_RELEASE
27. `submit()` refuses unless every RESULTING line (kept, changed, added) names a
    treatment billed at exactly its branch tariff in force on the INVOICE's clinical
    date, with no discount: `CORRECTION_TARIFF_FREE_TEXT`, `CORRECTION_TARIFF_UNVERIFIED`,
    `CORRECTION_TARIFF_PRICE_MISMATCH`, `CORRECTION_TARIFF_DISCOUNT`. Independent of
    the branch mode: a transitional branch may correct INTO tariff authority, never out.
28. Approve and apply re-check it under the lock; a moved/withdrawn tariff ⇒ STALE
    `TARIFF_AUTHORITY_CHANGED`. Applied lines get `TARIFF_MATCHED` provenance.
29. Corrections never carry exceptions (undecided). Rp0 refusals (rule 190 §10) unchanged.

## 8. Tariff provisioning & audit — IMPLEMENTED_THIS_RELEASE
30. Master-data tariff create/update/delete are audited `RME_TARIFF_CREATED|UPDATED|DELETED`
    (ids, cents, dates, flags — never `notes`) inside their transaction.
31. `rme:tariff-template --branch=` prints an import-ready CSV (price blank, tariff in
    force for reference). `rme:tariff-import <csv> --branch= --effective-date=` is a
    DRY RUN unless `--apply --confirm-plan=<digest> --actor= --reason=`; the plan is
    recomputed in the transaction (drift refuses); the whole plan is refused on any
    unknown/inactive treatment, duplicate code, non-positive / >2-decimal price, or a
    CONFLICT with an existing tariff at that date (never overwritten — edit through
    master data); only CREATE rows are written, each audited `RME_TARIFF_IMPORTED`;
    re-running is idempotent. Actor needs `manage_clinic_master_data`.
   **[SUPERSEDED in part by rule 193 §3 (FEATURE-RME-BRANCH-TARIFF-PROVISIONING-1):
   `--apply` now also REQUIRES `--approval-reference`, bound into the digest;
   CREATE rows record approval provenance; an identical-price tariff without
   provenance is ATTESTED (price untouched); master-data edits of price/date/
   treatment withdraw the approval. Create-only and CONFLICT are unchanged.]**
32. **An empty successful import is not evidence that a branch is priced.**

## 9. Readiness — IMPLEMENTED_THIS_RELEASE
33. `rme:tariff-authority-readiness [--json] [--strict]` — read-only per RME branch:
    mode, readiness, tariffed/active, missing and zero codes, billed lines by
    provenance. FAIL (exit 1): a strict branch not ready, or a strict code naming no
    RME branch. WATCH (exit 1 only with --strict): any branch transitional.
    **[Extended by rule 193 §5: `provenance`, `approved_tariffs`,
    `unverified_tariff_codes`, `strict_eligible`; WATCH
    `TARIFF_PROVENANCE_UNVERIFIED`, FAIL `STRICT_BRANCH_TARIFF_PROVENANCE_UNVERIFIED`.]**

## 10. Roles, oversight, scope — unchanged
34. Finance Klinik and Data Analyst stay READ-ONLY; the laboratory `Finance` role gains
    nothing; no role gains a correction or exception permission. Branch isolation of
    cashier/correction is unchanged (`RmeWorkingBranchScope`).
35. `FEATURE_RME_INVOICE_CORRECTION` stays **OFF**. This rule is not activation.

## 11. Tests, deploy, verification, activation
36. Suites `tests/Feature/RmeTariffAuthority/*` (token `RmeTariffAuthority`) and the
    new `tests/Feature/RmeInvoiceCorrection/RmeInvoiceCorrection{PaymentBlock,TariffAuthority}Test`
    are declared in `config/ci_runner.php` `critical_gate_mandatory_suites`. The D10
    races live in the PostgreSQL concurrency suite (skips on SQLite, runs in CI).
37. Deploy: one additive migration (nullable provenance columns, no backfill) +
    `PermissionSeeder` (two permissions, no grant). No RoleSeeder change. Rollback is
    a code rollback; the columns can stay (nullable, unread by older code).
38. Production verification is read-only: tariffs unchanged, all branches TRANSITIONAL,
    exceptions OFF, flag OFF, invoice/payment totals unchanged. Never create a fake
    invoice or payment to "prove" pricing or D10.
39. Strict enforcement for a branch needs: the owner's official tariff list imported
    (D21h), `rme:tariff-authority-readiness` READY for it, an explicit config change,
    and a supervised window. **[Rule 193: "READY" here means `strict_eligible = true`
    — TARIFF_READY AND every tariff in force carrying approval provenance.]** Correction activation additionally needs rule 191 §20.
